      "side": 1,
      "message": "All this CL changes to the codeflow is turn\n```\nif (cond) { X }\nelse if (cond) { X}\nelse { Y }\n```\ninto \n```\nif (cond) { X }\nelse { Y }\n```\n\nAs, previously, we had:\n\n- if `get_loaded_vcpu` returned `NULL`, the handler branched to `hyp_panic()`;\n- otherwise, it branched to `__guest_exit_panic()` which:\n  - if `get_loaded_vcpu` returned `NULL`, branched to `hyp_panic()`;\n  - otherwise, returned [*] to `hyp_panic()`.\n\nand now, the handler branches to `__hyp_panic()` (i.e. `__guest_exit_panic()` renamed) directly.\n\n[*] in detail, `__guest_exit_panic()`/`__hyp_panic()` (see `arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/entry.S`)\n\n1. L103: points the saved LR in `kvm_hyp_ctxt` to `hyp_panic`\n1. L155: restores LR from `kvm_hyp_ctxt`\n1. L168/L174/L199/L213: `ret`urns, effectively jumping to `hyp_panic()`",
